OL,3,GNEWSAMore trans-inclusive spaces
OL,4,Aplanned for city
OL,5,
OL,6,FTransgender people living in Oxford
OL,7,Fwill be better supported to access
OL,8,Ffacilities like public toilets under
OL,9,Fplans agreed this week.
OL,11,FAt an Oxford City Council meeting,
OL,12,Fcouncillors voted in favour of
OL,13,Fproviding more inclusive spaces,
OL,14,Fincluding gender-neutral facilities.
OL,16,FIt comes after updated guidance from
OL,17,Fthe Equality and Human Rights
OL,18,FCommission (EHRC) stated that
OL,19,Ftransgender people using single-sex
OL,20,Ffacilities should do so based on their
OL,21,Fbiological sex.
OL,23,APub: 08-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
